---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CountryMap from '../components/CountryMap.astro';
import FilmStrip from '../components/FilmStrip.astro';

// Adventure photos (optimized, GPS/metadata stripped) in public/adventure/.
// Curated + ordered to avoid similar-looking neighbors (see .tmp-optimize-adventure
// selection when regenerating). Alt text is generic; David can supply descriptions.
const travelPhotos = Array.from({ length: 14 }, (_, i) => ({
  src: `/adventure/travel-${i + 1}.jpg`,
  alt: `Travel photo ${i + 1}`,
}));
const climbingPhotos = Array.from({ length: 16 }, (_, i) => ({
  src: `/adventure/climbing-${i + 1}.jpg`,
  alt: `Climbing and mountaineering photo ${i + 1}`,
}));
const snowboardingPhotos = Array.from({ length: 16 }, (_, i) => ({
  src: `/adventure/snowboarding-${i + 1}.jpg`,
  alt: `Snowboarding photo ${i + 1}`,
}));
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Adventure - David Goodloe"
  description="Life outside work - rock climbing and mountaineering, snowboarding, and traveling to 14 countries and counting, mapped and photographed."
>
  <h1>Adventure</h1>

  <p class="lede">I love finding myself in "improbable places". And (ask anyone who's traveled with me) I usually say that phrase aloud when I'm in a spot where that idea strikes me. Whether I'm 500-ft off the ground on a cliff ledge that only a handful of humans have ever stood on before, or in an off-the-beaten-path restaurant in a small town in a foreign country, these are the kinds of places and experiences that bring me joy.</p>

  {/* Interactive map. Travel + Climbing = shaded countries (world map). Mountaineering +
      Snowboarding = destination dots on a detailed US map. Mountaineering status: summit
      (green) or attempt (yellow). */}
  <CountryMap
    visited={["us", "pr", "bs", "es", "gb", "gr", "cz", "fr", "nl", "mx", "au", "br", "no"]}
    climbed={["us", "mx", "br", "no"]}
    mountaineering={[
      { name: "Mount Baker", lat: 48.7767, lng: -121.8144, status: "summit", nudge: [18, 16] },
      { name: "Mount Shuksan", lat: 48.8306, lng: -121.6022, status: "summit" },
      { name: "Mount Olympus", lat: 47.8014, lng: -123.7065, status: "summit", nudge: [12, 0] },
      { name: "Mount Rainier", lat: 46.8523, lng: -121.7603, status: "attempt" },
      { name: "Midsummer Dome, WY", lat: 42.77, lng: -109.21, status: "summit" },
    ]}
    snowboarding={[
      { name: "Sugar Mountain, NC", lat: 36.1329, lng: -81.8637 },
      { name: "Beech Mountain, NC", lat: 36.2019, lng: -81.8873 },
      { name: "Appalachian Ski Mtn, NC", lat: 36.1586, lng: -81.6936 },
      { name: "Cataloochee, NC", lat: 35.5945, lng: -83.0876 },
      { name: "Wolf Ridge, NC", lat: 35.9758, lng: -82.6361 },
      { name: "Snowshoe Mountain, WV", lat: 38.4121, lng: -79.9953 },
      { name: "Copper Mountain, CO", lat: 39.5022, lng: -106.1517 },
      { name: "Keystone, CO", lat: 39.6084, lng: -105.9437 },
      { name: "Breckenridge, CO", lat: 39.4783, lng: -106.0667 },
      { name: "Vail, CO", lat: 39.6061, lng: -106.355 },
      { name: "Beaver Creek, CO", lat: 39.6042, lng: -106.5165 },
      { name: "Bridger Bowl, MT", lat: 45.8179, lng: -110.9066 },
    ]}
  />

  <h2>Travel</h2>
  <p>
    I want to see and visit as much of the world as possible in this life. I'm no
    van-life nomad or jet-setting freelancer (at least not yet ;)). But hopefully this
    page is proof that you can hold down a full-time job in a home-base city and still
    get out there in the world.
  </p>
  <p>
    14 countries and counting!
  </p>
  <FilmStrip images={travelPhotos} label="Travel photos" />

  <h2>Climbing &amp; mountaineering</h2>
  <p>
    Climbing has given me some of my favorite memories and adventures of my entire
    life. It's a great excuse to travel to parts of the world that others rarely visit,
    but which have a lot to offer the visitor. And there is no more improbable place
    than standing on a glaciated mountain summit or clinging to an overhanging cliff-face.
  </p>
  <p class="section-link">
    <a href="https://www.mountainproject.com/user/201008756/david-goodloe" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Mountain Project &rarr;
    </a>
  </p>
  <FilmStrip images={climbingPhotos} label="Climbing and mountaineering photos" />

  <h2>Snowboarding</h2>
  <p>
    I've often said that snowboarding is the most fun I've ever had on my own two feet.
    It's true, and if you've ever ridden, you know the feeling yourself. Living in the
    southeast US, I certainly don't get to snowboard as much as I get to do some of my
    other adventures, but we still make time for it. It's such an incredible way to move
    through mountainous terrain, even if the lift did the hard part for you (unless it
    didn't... see splitboarding!).
  </p>
  <FilmStrip images={snowboardingPhotos} label="Snowboarding photos" />
</BaseLayout>
